1
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:28,500
A visual and musical journey through time

2
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:51,000
Chronos is a documentary film directed by Ron Fricke.

3
00:16:07,500 --> 00:16:13,500
Carefully picked scenes of nature and civilization are viewed at high speed using time-lapse
cinematography in an effort to demonstrate the history of various regions.

4
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:36,000
Chronos ( KRON-ohs) is a 1985 non-narrative documentary film directed and
photographed by Ron Fricke, with music by Michael Stearns.

5
00:26:52,500 --> 00:26:58,500
Shot on IMAX film in eight countries, it consists primarily of
time-lapse footage captured with custom-built cameras.

6
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:21,000
Originally released in IMAX theaters in May 1985, it has since been
made available on VHS, DVD, HD DVD, and Blu-ray.

7
00:37:37,500 --> 00:37:43,500
The film explores themes of nature, time lapse photography, poetic documentary.
